	(text "THE CONSOLE UART, ITS CLOCK, THE RS-232 DRIVER, THE DB9, THE TTL HEADER, THE UART'S -INT" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "54c0b7f4-fae3-56b7-82f6-9bd5dfce7f67"))
	(text "IC1 is selected by IO-SELDATA (a P1 access) AND UART-CS, its register by UART-A0-2: all from the control latch.\nOSC1, 1.8432 MHz: divisor 3 is 38400 baud. TX goes to the MAX232 and to the TTL header J2; JP2 picks where RX comes\nfrom. JP1 puts the MAX232's two lines on the DB9's pins 2 and 3, either way round. The UART's INT reaches the bus\n-INT through IC8/F and JP7: with JP7 off the card never touches -INT." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c158dce9-f4e6-566f-9f57-3394f5e83f9e"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
